{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Two hundred she-goats</b> — the entire verse ends in mem, and likewise the verse ומנחתם ונסכיהם — because the animals he sent to Esau are 450 offerings in the year, excluding the daily offerings, as explained in the portion of Pinchas. And they are 8 in number, and corresponding to them reigned eight kings in Edom before there reigned a king in Israel. Another interpretation: therefore everything ends in mem, because all the animals he sent him were blemished, so that he would not offer from them an offering."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The phrase ומנחתם ונסכיהם is quoted unaddressed; it is Numbers 28:–29 (the offerings catalogue in the Pinchas portion). The '450 offerings' and '8 in number' are preserved as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:35.415541637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}